  "term": "acquisitiveness",
  "definition": "In this historical psychology usage, acquisitiveness can mean either a tendency to take possession of things and treat them as one’s own, or an inborn ease in gaining new knowledge or learning. The term was used for both ownership-seeking and natural learnability.",
